ricci-scalar-for-anti-de-sitter-space.conceptual_definition:
The Ricci scalar $R$ for a maximally symmetric Lorentzian manifold with negative constant sectional curvature is obtained by contracting the Riemann curvature tensor $R_{\mu
uho\sigma} = - rac{1}{L^2}(g_{\muho}g_{
u\sigma} - g_{\mu\sigma}g_{
uho})$. Double contraction with the metric tensor $g^{\mu
u}$ yields the constant scalar curvature $R = - rac{d(d-1)}{L^2}$, where $d$ is the spacetime dimension and $L$ is the $AdS$ radius of curvature.

ricci-scalar-for-anti-de-sitter-space.interpretation:
The equation $R = - rac{d(d-1)}{L^2}$ relates the scalar curvature $R$ of Anti-de Sitter spacetime directly to its dimension $d$ and its characteristic curvature radius $L$. The overall negative sign reflects the hyperbolic, negatively curved geometry of $AdS$. The quadratic dimensional factor $d(d-1)$ originates from the trace algebra over $d$ spacetime dimensions when contracting $g^{\muho}g^{
u\sigma}(g_{\muho}g_{
u\sigma} - g_{\mu\sigma}g_{
uho}) = d^2 - d = d(d-1)$. The factor $1/L^2$ provides the correct canonical dimension of inverse length squared ($[L^{-2}]$).

tensor-transformation-contravariant.conceptual_definition:
In pseudo-Riemannian geometry and general relativity, raising an index is the musical isomorphism $(\sharp)$ applied to a covariant slot of a tensor. For a mixed rank-2 tensor $T^\mu_{\ \alpha} \in \mathcal{T}^1_1(M)$, contraction with the contravariant (inverse) metric tensor $g^{
u\alpha}$ yields the components of the fully contravariant rank-2 tensor $T^{\mu\nu} \in \mathcal{T}^2_0(M)$ according to $T^{\mu\nu} = g^{
u\alpha} T^\mu_{\ \alpha}$.

tensor-transformation-contravariant.limits_and_boundary:
In flat spacetime (Minkowski space), the metric tensor $g^{
u\alpha}$ reduces to the constant Minkowski metric $\eta^{
u\alpha} = \operatorname{diag}(-1, 1, 1, 1)$ (or $(+1, -1, -1, -1)$ depending on signature convention).
